==Old English==

===Etymology===
{{root|ang|ine-pro|*gʷʰen-}}
From {{inh|ang|gmw-pro|*gunþi}}, from {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*gunþiz}}, from {{der|ang|ine-pro|*gʷʰéntis||killing, blow}}. Shifted into the ō-stems at some point before i-umlaut; the inherited form ''*gȳþ'' occurs as the final element of names.

Germanic cognates include {{cog|non|gunnr}} ~ {{m|non|guðr}}. {{w|Old Saxon}} ''gūđ-'' and {{w|Old High German}} ''gund-'' appear in compounds.

